        "ggrpx59fHRV_text": "How Fasting Can Support You Through Menopause",
        "ggxD5F8ssSO_text": "<p><strong>Managing Menopausal Weight Gain with Fasting</strong></p><p>Menopause often brings with it an unwelcome side effect—weight gain that seems stubborn and hard to shake. This is due to hormonal changes that slow down <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2748330/\"><u>metabolism</u></a> and increase fat storage, particularly around the abdomen. However, fasting, when done correctly, can be a powerful tool for managing this weight gain, helping you regain control of your body and feel your best.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>How Fasting Helps</strong></p><p>Intermittent fasting, one of the most popular methods, involves cycling between periods of eating and fasting. This approach can help reduce overall <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30172870/\"><u>calorie intake</u></a> while boosting your body’s ability to burn fat. During fasting periods, your insulin levels drop, which encourages the body to tap into stored fat for energy. This process can be particularly beneficial during menopause when <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16051710/\"><u>insulin sensitivity</u></a> tends to decrease, making weight gain more likely.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Fasting also triggers a process known as autophagy, where the body cleans out damaged cells and regenerates new ones. This not only aids in weight management but also enhances overall health and longevity, making it an excellent practice during the menopausal transition.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Adapting Fasting to Your Needs</strong></p><p>It’s important to remember that menopause is a unique time in a woman’s life, and what works for one person might not work for another. Fasting can be tailored to fit your specific needs and lifestyle. For instance, you might start with a 12-hour fasting window and gradually increase it as your body adapts. Listening to your body is key—if you feel overly fatigued or notice negative changes, it’s important to adjust your approach.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To enhance the benefits of fasting and support your overall health during menopause, consider incorporating natural supplements like Wellness Nest’s Shilajit into your routine. <a href=\"https://wellnessnest.co/blogs/news/what-is-ayurveda-principles-of-ayurvedic-medicine-and-its-holistic-approach\"><u>Shilajit</u></a> is packed with fulvic acid and essential minerals that can help regulate hormones, increase energy levels, and support your body’s natural fat-burning processes. By combining the power of fasting with the nourishing benefits of Shilajit, you can take charge of your weight and well-being during menopause.</p><p><span style=\"color:#1B8D17;\"><strong><u>=&gt; </u></strong></span><a href=\"https://wellnessnest.co/blogs/news/shed-the-menopause-pounds-secrets-to-keeping-weight-off-for-good\"><span style=\"color:#1B8D17;\"><strong><u>Tips to Keep Your Weight Off on Menopause</u></strong></span></a><span style=\"color:#1B8D17;\"><strong><u>.</u></strong></span></p>",
